A||||8||87FieroGTx||Lotus Esprit V8 sound from a Fiero? Part 2||||5||
Z||000000||87FieroGTx||11-27-2001||02:59 AM|||| I know I know..... I've asked a similar question about Ferrari sound from a Fiero but I bit off a bit to much on that one!<P> I think the Lotus sound would be MUCH easier to get with a domestic engine.<P> I want it to sound like this Lotus Esprit V8 or maybe even a bit mellower/smother.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/seanvideos/videos/seanV8.mpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/seanvideos/videos/seanV8.mpg</A> <P> My plans are to use my 3.2 V6 for now but eventually upgrade to a Northstar mated to a (286?) 5 speed.<P> Here's what I'm thinking of using.<P> 2.5" Stainless Steel Pipes all around<P> Stainless Steel Short/Long Headers (Any suggestions??)<P> Tubi or Brullen Muffler<P> Free Flow Cat<P> Lotus Resonator (Are these tips? or is it a separate unit? Where would I buy one of these???<P> And/Or ANSA or Brullen resonated 2" twin resonated tips <P> I want it to be quieter than stock but with that Lotus (Exotic) sound.<P><BR> ANY   TIPS   OR   CORRECTIONS   WOULD   BE   GREATLY   APPRECIATED!!!!!<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||87FieroGTx||11-27-2001||03:16 AM|||| Oh.. I forgot to add, I would like to avoid POPS and GURGLES when I let off the throttle at all costs.  There's nothing worse than that sound to me. When I let off the throttle I want a SMOOTH sound.||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||11-27-2001||04:02 AM||||Well, you picked the two production 180degree crank V8s in the world  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>They're fundamentally different inside, but the lotous V8 isn't quite in as high a state of tune as the Ferrari (the Ferrari V8 makes more HP/litre and hp peroid on the atmosphere than the lotous can manage with *twin turbos!*<P>Ferrari's is also 5valve (3intake) and the Lotus uses a 'conventional' DOHC design (with  a pair of turbos.)<P>You're on the right track to getting something close however.  I'd go absolutely no larger than 2" primaries, and think about 1&3/4s or even 1.5" on a small-chamber motor.<P>(this isn't a big-block after all, and we want *speed* and scavanging resonances up high, not low  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Mufflers will do the job, it's important not to skimp here.   Consider running two cats in paralell for *EACH* half of a dual exhaust. I'm going to try that (if I can fit it all.)<P>The Northstar's firing order is giving me a heck of a time in devising a 180degree *header* (with some primaries exchanging sides into opposite collectors. yeah.)<BR>I can't seem to do it with only two crosovers. Unless I'm crazy here.<P>PS: the gurgle is a natural side effect of an engine in a high state of tune, just don't spend a long time off the throttle if you don't like it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  (!!!!)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||87FieroGTx||11-27-2001||04:00 PM|||| Thank you Artherd, I'm almost ready to order the parts.<P> I still need to know if the Lotus resonators are TIPs or a separate unit?||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||11-28-2001||02:56 PM||||What makes you think this will make your car sound like a V8 Lotus?  That's like trying to make a Honda sound like a Fiero.  Just because you add lotus tips and a different muffler doesn't mean you have the Lotus sound.  Not trying to be an a$$hole or anything, but I guess it's too late.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icare.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||87FieroGTx||11-28-2001||03:34 PM|||| I don't want it to sound exactly like a Lotus, I just want a MORE Exotic sound.<P> I'm not a fan of loud (OPEN) exhaust. In my opinion Fieros sound nice but there a bit to loud. I want something more refined.||||reg||14
Z||000006||Master_Sushi||11-28-2001||04:09 PM||||Is it even possable to get an american pushrod to sound like an exotic DOHC engine? I love the low rumble of fieros, and thats what an OHV does best. I don't know..... I'm with GTB on this one. It would *suck* if you did all that work, and then it ended up sounding like a riced out civic.<p>[This message has been edited by Master_Sushi (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fieroX||11-28-2001||08:02 PM||||I am wanting an exotic sound from my car also.  I will have the 3800 supercharged v6 and im going with 1 3/4" primary headers, 2 1/2" collectors, 2 1/2" Y-pipe to 3" collector, single 3" exhaust into an 80 series flowmaster 3" inlet dual 2 1/2" outlet, with these tips.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://WWW.southfloridapulleyhq.com/images/products/ractive_tips00.JPG"> <BR>I have no idea what it will sound like, but I have a feeling that with about 340 horsepower and 15 lbs of boost blowing through these pipes, its going to sound pretty wicked.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
